prompt:
A Go HTTP handler calls this for every request:

```go
// Returning abandons the other sends.
func first(urls []string) string {
  ch := make(chan string)
  for _, u := range urls {
    go func(u string) {
      ch <- fetch(u)
    }(u)
  }
  return <-ch
}
```

Each call passes 4 URLs. Memory use rises steadily over days. Why?
